## Where the hallucinations really live

If a shared amplitude can only produce a line, how do you get a genuine two-dimensional disk? You must **break the factorization** — with directed edges or independent per-edge phases. Start from a symmetric graph (spectrum on the line) and inject asymmetry to watch the eigenvalues spill into the plane.

{{interactive_demo:2}}

